                <head>461. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>In a memorandum dated March 21, Thorsten V.
                        Kalijarvi requested Roy R. Rubottom,
                        Jr., to review the question of negotiating a settlement for
                    United States logistical support provided Colombia during the Korean conflict.
                    This memorandum was accompanied by a paper which reported on the legal basis for
                    settlement negotiations. (Department of State, Rubottom Files: Lot 59 D 573,
                    Colombia) In a memorandum of April 16 to Kalijarvi, Rubottom
                    recommended against the initiation of talks with Colombia on this issue. He
                    stated, “The Colombians would, in all likelihood, respond that they can pay
                    nothing. At present Colombia is confronted with an acute foreign <pb facs="0969"
                        n="935" xml:id="pg935"/> exchange shortage. In its external accounts it has
                    a large accumulation of commercial indebtedness.” Rubottom recommended that negotiations be undertaken at a later
                    time. (<hi rendition="#italic">Ibid</hi>.)</p>
            </div>
